* B-062 regression (repro: backlog/repro/a3-mlprobe-exact.cir): an MLPROBE matches its listed wavelengths
* within a relative 1e-12 and ignores the others. It used to print "received unsupported signal" on stdout for
* every such event; it now prints one warning per probe on stderr at the end of the run, in name order, with
* every digit needed. {lambda0}+1.5e-9 = 1.5514999999999999e-06 matches the listed 1.5515e-06: MLPROBE1 traces
* it (before PH, matching was exact and MLPROBE1 warned). MLPROBE0 lists 1.5600000001e-06, 6.4e-11 away from
* cwsrc1's 1.56e-06: not matched. MLPROBE2 is declared first, MLPROBE0 (declared last) warns first.
* MLPROBE3 lists every wavelength of its net: no warning.
.assign lambda0 = 1.55e-6
vlsrc1 a values=[[1e-12,1e-3,{lambda0}+1.5e-9],[2e-12,2e-3,]]
cwsrc1 b wl=1.56e-6 power=1
merger1 a b m
mlprobe2 m wl=[1.56e-6]
mlprobe1 a wl=[1.5515e-6]
mlprobe3 b wl=[1.56e-6]
mlprobe0 b wl=[1.5600000001e-6]
.options traceall=0
.tran 5e-12
